            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0387" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/427: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-22T11:00:00+08:00">April 22, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 22—12:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 22, 11 a.m. I have received fairly reliable information that the
                            Chinese have purchased 50 Italian planes funds for which were obtained
                            from Italian Boxer indemnity. It is rumored that nine Italian mechanics
                            and aviators are now in Hangchow and that there is a possibility that H.
                            H. Kung who is now in charge of aviation matters may replace Colonel
                            Jouett and other American institutors [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >instructors</hi>] at the Central Aviation School with Italian
                            institutors.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
